bool is 4 bytes on Darwin ppc32. Keep these structures at their intended
sizes by storing flags as uint8_t, and skip the register-size assertions
that cannot hold with a 4-byte bool.

This includes the tag in mfbt's IsPackableVariant. With a bool tag,
small types such as Result<Ok, uint8_t enum> no longer fit in a word,
fall back to PackingStrategy::Variant and fail to compile wherever
mozilla/ResultVariant.h is not included (intl/components Locale.h).

